(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Correlations Between Main Metric and Median Efficiency\
\>", "Title"],

Cell["\<\
Spearman rank correlation between each training run's validation metric (CAP, threshold drift, W1 distance, or CVaR25 efficiency, per the run's strategy) and its median signal efficiency, over the training steps the two series share.

Inputs: notebooks/exported_metrics/<experiment>/<run>/val_summary_*.csv, exported from MLflow by notebooks/get_mlflow_corrs.py. Methods live in notebooks/lib/corrs_lib.wl. Nothing is exported; the result is the association displayed at the end.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"lib\", \"corrs_lib.wl\"}]];\
\>", "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Results\
\>", "Section"],

Cell["\<\
corrs[experiment][run] holds the run's method, the two CSV files used, and SpearmanRho (or a Missing[] explaining why it could not be computed). Metrics where smaller is better (Stable, W1) are sign-flipped first, so a positive rho always means \"better metric, better efficiency\".\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
corrs = ComputeAllCorrelations[\"exported_metrics\", True]\
\>", "Input"]
}, Open]]
}, Open]]
},
WindowSize->{1200, 900},
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)
